---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import { brand } from "../brand/config";
import "../styles/public-pages.css";
---

<Base
  title="FAQ"
  description={`Clear answers about ${brand.name}, the waitlist, cancellation, memory and optional services.`}
  canonicalPath="/faq/"
>
  <section class="pwy-page pwy-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div class="pwy-shell">
      <header class="pwy-hero">
        <p class="pwy-kicker">Questions / 05</p>
        <div class="pwy-hero__grid">
          <h1 id="faq-heading">The short answers.</h1>
          <p class="pwy-hero__lede">
            The product is unusual. The explanation should be plain. Open a question to see the
            exact arrangement.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pwy-hero__meta">
          <span class="pwy-stamp">Truth before theatre</span>
          <span>Waitlist open</span>
          <span>Paid membership closed</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="pwy-faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
        <details open>
          <summary>Is {brand.name} a real club?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              Yes. The membership relationship, the details you choose to share and the
              correspondence are real. Paid membership is currently closed; the public waitlist is
              free and does not start a membership.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I have to attend the events?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              No. Ordinary plans are made to be cancelled before their date. There is no RSVP,
              check-in or no-show, and nobody expects you to attend. A completely silent member is a
              successful member.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is the difference between the tiers?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              All three tiers provide equal belonging. Member, Corresponding Member and Deluxe
              Member differ in what can arrive and how much personal attention we can give: more
              mail, keepsakes, gifts or calls, when included and chosen by you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How often are plans made and cancelled?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              You choose the pace: occasional, about monthly, a couple per month, or our discretion.
              Invitations generally arrive 7–21 days before the date on them; cancellations
              generally arrive 12–36 hours before it. That is the plan working as promised.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What do you remember about me?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              Only what you choose to share. You can see, edit, restrict, mark as do-not-mention,
              export or remove those details through the member portal. Suggestions stay separate
              until you confirm them; we do not invent things about you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What about gifts, calls and physical mail?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              Each is off until you opt in. You can change your mind at any time; anything planned
              for the future stops, and the rest of your membership carries on.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is a manufactured commitment?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              A consensual artificial social obligation: you ask for a plausible scenario, confirm
              it, use the pressure toward a goal you chose, and we explicitly cancel it. You can
              abort at any time; nothing dangles.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is the appearance service?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              A separately priced service for a real person to appear in a harmless, agreed role. It
              is not bundled into any tier. Travel and substantial preparation are quoted
              separately, and prohibited or impersonating uses are refused.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Will my data be used to train AI?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              No. Member data is used to run {brand.name}; it is not exported to train general
              models. AI may help with a first draft, but it cannot override your choices or invent
              things about you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>When does paid membership open?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              The waitlist is open now, but paid membership and payments are not. We will write when
              there is a real next step; joining the list is free.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is the lore real?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              {brand.name} is a real membership relationship. Some characters, places and history in correspondence
              may be fictional. We do not represent fictional references as real partners, endorsements
              or bookings.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I leave or ask a question?</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              Members can cancel and request data removal through the member portal, subject to
              legitimate retention requirements. For a public question, join the waitlist and tell
              us what you need to know.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>

      <footer class="pwy-page-footer">
        <p>Still unsure? A human can answer the question behind the question.</p>
        <a class="pwy-button" href="/waiting-list/"
          >Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </footer>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pwy-page {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .pwy-hero {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 7rem) 0 clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .pwy-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font: 600 0.72rem/1.2 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .pwy-hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(16rem, 0.9fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 9rem);
    align-items: end;
  }
  .pwy-hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  .pwy-hero__lede {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.8vw, 1.45rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .pwy-hero__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font: 0.72rem/1.2 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .pwy-stamp {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .pwy-faq-list {
    max-width: 58rem;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 0;
  }
  .pwy-faq-list details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .pwy-faq-list details:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .pwy-faq-list summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 1.35rem 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font: 400 clamp(1.25rem, 2.3vw, 1.7rem)/1.15 var(--font-serif);
  }
  .pwy-faq-list summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .pwy-faq-list summary::after {
    content: "+";
    color: var(--accent);
    font: 1.2rem/1 var(--font-mono);
  }
  .pwy-faq-list details[open] summary::after {
    content: "−";
  }
  .pwy-faq-list details > div {
    padding: 0 3rem 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .pwy-faq-list p {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .pwy-page-footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 2rem 0 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .pwy-page-footer p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .pwy-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .pwy-button:hover,
  .pwy-button:focus-visible {
    background: var(--accent-secondary);
    color: #fff;
  }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .pwy-hero__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .pwy-faq-list details > div {
      padding-right: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
